# Repository-level ignore rules for the MP1 submission.
#
# `code/.gitignore` is a supplied, integrity-checked file and is left byte-identical; it already
# ignores `runs/` and `*.pt`. The rules here cover everything else, so that the repository holds
# only what is needed to reproduce the recorded score (1.700525 test BPB) and to check the
# report's numbers. Files under `code/runs/` that are kept as evidence are added explicitly
# (`git add -f`), because the supplied rules exclude that whole directory.

# OS and editor byproducts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.trae/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python byproducts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch output
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak

# Submission bundle build output. The bundle is uploaded with the website submission rather
# than committed, because the frozen checkpoint it carries is already tracked inside the
# repository and duplicating it would add 4 MB for nothing.
dist/

# Per-window loss arrays: regenerated by evaluate.py on every scoring run
*.window-nll.npy

# Agent scaffolding: records how the work was arranged, not how to reproduce it
.specify/
history/